  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the primary uncertainty is whether a standard multimodal multiprofile pipeline can establish a strong performance baseline. Config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA n2000, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted fusion) uses well-established, robust components across all design axes, minimizing the risk of a poor result due to a single weak choice. It tests the core hypothesis that combining RNA and image modalities with multiprofile aggregation yields competitive accuracy. Establishing this baseline is critical: if it performs well, subsequent experiments can systematically upgrade individual components (e.g., swap to ViT-L, transformer aggregation, scvi/scgpt encoders) to identify what drives gains; if it underperforms, it flags that the basic multimodal architecture needs rethinking. As experiment 1 of 10, this maximizes information per trial by anchoring the search around a reliable reference point."
}

